1
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
An offer you can't refuse.

2
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:46,000
The Godfather is a drama, crime film directed by Francis Ford Coppola.

3
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Spanning the years 1945 to 1955, a chronicle of the
fictional Italian-American Corleone crime family.

4
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
When organized crime family patriarch, Vito Corleone barely survives an attempt on his life, his youngest son,
Michael steps in to take care of the would-be killers, launching a campaign of bloody revenge.

5
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:16,000
Don Vito Corleone, played by Marlon Brando.

6
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Michael Corleone, played by Al Pacino.

7
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:56,000
Sonny Corleone, played by James Caan.

8
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Tom Hagen, played by Robert Duvall.

9
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Clemenza, played by Richard S. Castellano.

10
00:58:20,000 --> 00:58:26,000
Kay Adams, played by Diane Keaton.

11
01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
The Godfather is a 1972 American epic gangster film directed by Francis Ford Coppola, who
co-wrote the screenplay with Mario Puzo based on Puzo's best-selling 1969 novel.

12
01:10:00,000 --> 01:10:06,000
The film features an ensemble cast that includes Marlon Brando, Al Pacino, James Caan, Richard
Castellano, Robert Duvall, Sterling Hayden, John Marley, Richard Conte and Diane Keaton.

13
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:56,000
It is the first installment in The Godfather trilogy, which chronicles the Corleone family under patriarch Vito Corleone (Brando) and
the transformation of his youngest son, Michael Corleone (Pacino), from reluctant family outsider to ruthless mafia boss.

14
01:21:40,000 --> 01:21:46,000
Paramount Pictures obtained the rights to the novel for
$80,000, before it gained popularity.

15
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:36,000
Studio executives had trouble finding a director; the first few candidates turned down the position before Coppola signed on to direct
the film, but disagreement followed over casting several characters, in particular Vito (Brando) and Michael (Pacino).

16
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:26,000
Filming took place primarily in locations around New York City and
Sicily, and it was completed ahead of schedule.

17
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:16,000
The score was composed principally by Nino Rota, with
additional pieces by Carmine Coppola.

18
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:06,000
The Godfather premiered at the Loew's State Theatre on March 14, 1972, and
was widely released in the United States on March 24, 1972.

19
01:50:50,000 --> 01:50:56,000
It was the highest-grossing film of 1972, and was for a time the highest-grossing film
ever made, earning between $250 and $291 million at the box office.

20
01:56:40,000 --> 01:56:46,000
The film was acclaimed by critics and audiences, who praised its performances—particularly those of Brando and
Pacino—direction, screenplay, story, cinematography, editing, score, and portrayal of the mafia.

21
02:02:30,000 --> 02:02:36,000
The Godfather launched the successful careers of Coppola, Pacino,
and other relative newcomers in the cast and crew.

22
02:08:20,000 --> 02:08:26,000
At the 45th Academy Awards, the film won Best Picture, Best Actor
(Brando), and Best Adapted Screenplay (for Puzo and Coppola).

23
02:14:10,000 --> 02:14:16,000
In addition, the seven other Oscar nominations included Pacino, Caan, and
Duvall, all for Best Supporting Actor, and Coppola for Best Director.

24
02:20:00,000 --> 02:20:06,000
The Godfather is regarded as one of the greatest and most influential
films ever made, as well as a landmark of the gangster genre.

25
02:25:50,000 --> 02:25:56,000
It was selected for preservation in the U.S.

26
02:31:40,000 --> 02:31:46,000
National Film Registry of the Library of Congress in 1990, being deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant"
and is ranked the second-greatest film in American cinema (behind Citizen Kane) by the American Film Institute.

27
02:37:30,000 --> 02:37:36,000
It was followed by sequels The Godfather Part II
(1974) and The Godfather Part III (1990).

28
02:43:20,000 --> 02:43:26,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, loss of
loved one, love at first sight, italy, gangster.

29
02:49:10,000 --> 02:49:16,000
The tone is emotional.
